SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  AUTHOR  = 'A.Anand '                                                            SURVEY  = 'DESI    '                                                            DR      = '1       '                                                            ABSORBER= 'CIV     '           / Absorber name                                  KERWIDTH= '[3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]' / Kernel width in pixels (ker_width_pixels)      COEFFSIG=                    2 / sigma threshold (coeff_sigma)                  MULTRE  =                    1 / Multiplicative factor for residuals (mult_resi)D_PIX   =                  0.5 / tolerance for line separation (in Ang) (d_pix) PM_PIXEL=                  200 / N_Pixel for noise estimation (pm_pixel)        SN_LINE1=                    3 / S/N threshold for first line (sn_line1)        SN_LINE2=                    2 / S/N threshold for second line (sn_line2)       EWCOVAR =                    F / Use covariance for EW error (use_covariance)   LOGWAVE =                    F / Use log wavelength scaling (logwave)           LAM_ESEP=                   12 / lambda edges to avoid noisy regions (lam_edge_sNUMPY   = '1.21.6  '           / numpy version                                  ASTROPY = '5.1     '           / astropy version                                SCIPY   = '1.9.1   '           / scipy version                                  NUMBA   = '0.55.1  '           / numba version                                  QSOABFI = '1.0.5.dev20+g9c9d4e4.d20250416' / qsoabsfind version                 MATPLOT = '3.5.2   '           / matplotlib version                             END                                                                             